            <h3 data-number="4.4.1" id="descriptive-metadata-1"><span
            class="header-section-number">4.4.1</span> Descriptive
            Metadata</h3>
            <p><a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#descriptiveMetadata"><strong>Descriptive
            Metadata</strong></a> in LIDO hold information about the
            properties of the described object itself, whether it is
            analog or digital. These data are essential for searching,
            finding, and identifying the object in collections or
            portals. Descriptive information about an object or work
            includes the following four information areas:</p>
            <ol type="1">
            <li><strong>Object Classification</strong></li>
            <li><strong>Object Identification</strong></li>
            <li><strong>Event</strong></li>
            <li><strong>Object Relation</strong></li>
            </ol>
            <h4 data-number="4.4.1.1" id="object-classification"><span
            class="header-section-number">4.4.1.1</span> Object
            Classification</h4>
            <p>The <a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#objectClassificatio